  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed subdivision of the garden and associated erection of new boundary fencing would appear unduly out of character with the established pattern of rear gardens within the locality resulting in an incongruous and unsympathetic form of development. The public benefit of providing an additional residential unit does not outweigh the harm outlined above. The development would thereby be contrary to Policies D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD 6, DMD 7, DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014) as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed unit, by reason of its poor internal head heights would provide prospective occupants with a substandard form of accommodation, to the detriment of their overall living conditions. In addition, means of access through the garden of the main building at No. 100 Bullsmoor Lane would result in an undue loss of privacy afforded to the rear garden of this property, compromising the standard of residential amenity provided to occupants of this HMO. The public benefit of providing an additional residential unit does not outweigh the harm outlined above.  The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 6 DMD 7, DMD 8 and DMD 9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), as well as aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its poor access arrangements with occupants having to access the proposed flat through a narrow side walkway and through the garden of the main building at No. 100 Bullsmoor Lane, would result in a contrived and substandard form of development with inadequate means of access for prospective occupants. The limited width of the side accessway would also restrict independent access for the delivery of large goods demonstrating that the outbuilding is not suitable for use as independent living accommodation. The public benefit of providing an additional residential unit does not outweigh the harm outlined above. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies D3, D4 and D5 of the London Plan (2021) Policy CP4 of the Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD6 and DMD 8 of the Development Management Document (2014), as well as aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024)."
  ],
